{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BringConeSplitChirality","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BringConeSplitChirality","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.BringConeSplit"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.commutes_span_scalar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.commutes_span_scalar","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeSplitChirality.lean#L174-L186","doc":"**A left multiplication `L_u` that commutes with every element of a set `S` whose span\ncontains `i` and `j` is a scalar.** On the link `SL(2)/Γ₄`, `L_u` is well defined exactly\nwhen `u` commutes with `Γ₄`. So if `Γ₄` spans (Borel density, a hypothesis here), the\nsecond complex structure of the Hopf model does not descend: the commutant of the triad\nleaves only scalars. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.scalar_of_comm_sI_sJ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.scalar_of_comm_sI_sJ","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeSplitChirality.lean#L156-L172","doc":"Commuting with `i` and `j` forces `u` to be a scalar, when `2` is cancellable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.commSubmodule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.commSubmodule","kind":"def","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeSplitChirality.lean#L145-L154","doc":"The elements commuting with `u` form a submodule. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.M_i_flips_M_j_eigen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.M_i_flips_M_j_eigen","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeSplitChirality.lean#L134-L141","doc":"**`M_i` exchanges the two `M_j`-chiralities**: it sends an `M_j = s` eigenvector to an\n`M_j = −s` eigenvector. With `M_j` as the grading (`M_j_sq`) and `M_i` as the flip, this is\nV10's shape (flip free on rays, grading odd), using only the Reeb triad. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.M_i_anticomm_M_k","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.M_i_anticomm_M_k","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeSplitChirality.lean#L130-L132","doc":"`M_i` anticommutes with `M_k` too. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.M_i_anticomm_M_j","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.M_i_anticomm_M_j","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeSplitChirality.lean#L126-L128","doc":"**`M_i` anticommutes with `M_j`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.M_i_ray_free","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.M_i_ray_free","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeSplitChirality.lean#L112-L124","doc":"**`M_i` has no eigen-ray** unless `c² + 1 = 0`: whenever `−1` is not a square in `R`\nand scalars cancel, `M_i` fixes no ray. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.M_k_not_ray_free","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.M_k_not_ray_free","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeSplitChirality.lean#L105-L108","doc":"The same for `M_k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.M_j_not_ray_free","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.M_j_not_ray_free","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeSplitChirality.lean#L98-L103","doc":"**`M_j` has an eigen-ray**, eigenvalue `1`. So the Hopf-model choice `ι = M_j` is not\nfixed-point free on rays of the split model, and V10's `free_of_reeb_odd_grading` rules it\nout as a chirality flip there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.one_add_sK_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.one_add_sK_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeSplitChirality.lean#L93-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.one_add_sJ_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.one_add_sJ_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeSplitChirality.lean#L88-L91","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.M_k_fixes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.M_k_fixes","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeSplitChirality.lean#L84-L86","doc":"**`M_k` fixes `1 + k`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.M_j_fixes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.M_j_fixes","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeSplitChirality.lean#L80-L82","doc":"**`M_j` fixes `1 + j`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.M_k_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.M_k_sq","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeSplitChirality.lean#L74-L76","doc":"`M_k² = id`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.M_j_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.M_j_sq","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeSplitChirality.lean#L69-L72","doc":"`M_j² = id`: the geodesic-flow generator is an involution on vectors, unlike the\nHopf model's `reebM_j_sq`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.M_i_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.M_i_sq","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeSplitChirality.lean#L65-L67","doc":"`M_i² = −id`: the fibre rotation has order four, like the Hopf model. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.sK","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.sK","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeSplitChirality.lean#L60-L61","doc":"The split unit `k = ij` (`k² = +1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.sJ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.sJ","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeSplitChirality.lean#L58-L59","doc":"The split unit `j` (`j² = +1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.sI","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.sI","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeSplitChirality.lean#L56-L57","doc":"The split unit `i` (`i² = −1`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}